<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE HermitCrabInput SYSTEM "HermitCrabInput.dtd">
<HermitCrabInput>
  <Language>
    <Name>RightToLeftMetathesisReversal</Name>
    <!-- Synthetic construct-shaped mimic (docs/conformance/representative-typology-basis.md
         S1.2.4 - "Metathesis - right-to-left direction"; openspec/changes/
         plan-construct-coverage-completion task 4.6; docs/conformance/needs-decision-resolutions.md
         row 8). Invented CV roots only, no natural-language lexemes.

         Structural shape: one MetathesisRuleDef, multipleApplicationOrder="rightToLeftIterative",
         whose StructuralDescription is TWO adjacent SimpleContext switch positions, each a
         TWO-member natural class ({q,r} / {s,t}) - mirrors
         rust/crates/pg-foma/tests/phase_c_metathesis.rs's own MULTI_MEMBER_XML fixture (the
         per-branch literal cross-product precision witness), declared Dir::RightToLeft instead of
         the default Dir::LeftToRight that file already covers.

         Before openspec/changes/plan-construct-coverage-completion task 4.6,
         `crate::replace::compile_metathesis_rule` returned `Ok(None)` unconditionally for
         `Dir::RightToLeft` (an honest-unsupported scope boundary, not a wrong compile). Task 4.6
         built the SAME mirror-and-reverse construction `compile_rtl_branch_net` already uses for
         RTL *rewrite* rules (reverse the pattern's own slot order, remap the two switch indices to
         their mirrored positions, run the existing swap construction on the mirror, `fsm_reverse`
         the result, and `fsm_union` with the plain/LeftToRight-style net) - see
         `rust/crates/pg-foma/src/replace.rs`'s module doc, "Metathesis" section, and
         `crate::capability::MetathesisFaithfulSwapPredicate`'s own doc for the disposition
         (`ConfirmOnly`, never `Admit` - the union is a proven SUPERSET of the true RTL relation,
         not proven exact).

         Empirical finding while authoring this fixture (rust/crates/pg-foma tests, deleted
         throwaway probe): `pg_rules::metathesis::synthesize`'s own match-candidate selection
         (`match_candidates`'s ascending, direction-independent sort, in
         `rust/crates/pg-rules/src/metathesis.rs`) picks the LEFTMOST non-overlapping switch window
         regardless of `rule.dir`, for an overlapping-window probe - i.e. the real oracle is,
         empirically, direction-BLIND for metathesis today, the SAME shape
         `compile_rtl_branch_net`'s own doc found (before ITS OWN oracle fix) for ordinary
         `Iterative` rewrite rules. This grammar's own two lexical entries each have exactly ONE
         valid switch window (no overlap), so this empirical direction-blindness does not affect
         which surface each root resynthesizes to - oracle recall for BOTH roots here is identical
         to what the corresponding Dir::LeftToRight declaration would give. That is exactly why the
         FST-level "the construction genuinely differs from compiling as if LeftToRight" witness
         lives in `rust/crates/pg-foma/tests/phase_c_metathesis.rs` as a bare-automaton, oracle-free
         proof (mirroring `tests/phase_c_right_to_left.rs`'s own "aa -> b" worked example) rather
         than in this conformance fixture: this fixture's own job is the Stage-2 containment
         obligation (oracle recall subset-of FST propose), which holds regardless of whether the
         oracle happens to be direction-aware or -blind for the words it is asked about. -->
    <!-- G2a discipline (`conformance-staging/edge-cases/mpr-gated-exception`'s own authoring note):
         every segment needs a feature bundle that FULLY and UNIQUELY distinguishes it from every
         other segment, or a phonological-subrule reversal collapses feature-identical segments into
         a bracketed alternates class instead of the literal input string - the identical discipline
         `rust/crates/pg-foma/tests/phase_c_metathesis.rs`'s own fixtures already follow ("one
         distinct symbol value per segment"). -->
    <PartsOfSpeech>
      <PartOfSpeech id="posN"><Name>N</Name></PartOfSpeech>
    </PartsOfSpeech>
    <PhonologicalFeatureSystem>
      <SymbolicFeature id="featId">
        <Name>id</Name>
        <Symbols>
          <Symbol id="symQ">q</Symbol><Symbol id="symR">r</Symbol>
          <Symbol id="symS">s</Symbol><Symbol id="symT">t</Symbol>
        </Symbols>
      </SymbolicFeature>
    </PhonologicalFeatureSystem>
    <CharacterDefinitionTable id="t1">
      <Name>Main</Name>
      <SegmentDefinitions>
        <SegmentDefinition id="cQ"><Representations><Representation>q</Representation></Representations><FeatureValue feature="featId" symbolValues="symQ" /></SegmentDefinition>
        <SegmentDefinition id="cR"><Representations><Representation>r</Representation></Representations><FeatureValue feature="featId" symbolValues="symR" /></SegmentDefinition>
        <SegmentDefinition id="cS"><Representations><Representation>s</Representation></Representations><FeatureValue feature="featId" symbolValues="symS" /></SegmentDefinition>
        <SegmentDefinition id="cT"><Representations><Representation>t</Representation></Representations><FeatureValue feature="featId" symbolValues="symT" /></SegmentDefinition>
      </SegmentDefinitions>
    </CharacterDefinitionTable>
    <NaturalClasses>
      <SegmentNaturalClass id="ncSwitchA"><Name>SwitchA</Name><Segment segment="cQ" /><Segment segment="cR" /></SegmentNaturalClass>
      <SegmentNaturalClass id="ncSwitchB"><Name>SwitchB</Name><Segment segment="cS" /><Segment segment="cT" /></SegmentNaturalClass>
    </NaturalClasses>
    <PhonologicalRuleDefinitions>
      <MetathesisRule id="mrRtlReversal" leftSwitch="swB" rightSwitch="swA" multipleApplicationOrder="rightToLeftIterative">
        <Name>metathesisRtlReversal</Name>
        <StructuralDescription>
          <PhoneticTemplate>
            <PhoneticSequence>
              <SimpleContext id="swA" naturalClass="ncSwitchA" />
              <SimpleContext id="swB" naturalClass="ncSwitchB" />
            </PhoneticSequence>
          </PhoneticTemplate>
        </StructuralDescription>
      </MetathesisRule>
    </PhonologicalRuleDefinitions>
    <Strata>
      <Stratum characterDefinitionTable="t1" morphologicalRuleOrder="unordered" phonologicalRules="mrRtlReversal">
        <Name>Main</Name>
        <LexicalEntries>
          <LexicalEntry id="eRoot1">
            <Allomorphs><Allomorph id="aRoot1"><PhoneticShape>qs</PhoneticShape></Allomorph></Allomorphs>
            <MorphemeId>ROOT1</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>root1</Gloss>
          </LexicalEntry>
          <LexicalEntry id="eRoot2">
            <Allomorphs><Allomorph id="aRoot2"><PhoneticShape>rt</PhoneticShape></Allomorph></Allomorphs>
            <MorphemeId>ROOT2</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>root2</Gloss>
          </LexicalEntry>
        </LexicalEntries>
      </Stratum>
    </Strata>
  </Language>
</HermitCrabInput>
